    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and all tests pass (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`). AcceptanceTest is the only test class in the project.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `contactPreference` field is a read-only derived field on the `Owner` response, following the same pattern as the existing derived fields (`membershipLevel`, `locality`, `bulkSignupWarning`).\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `contactPreference` property to the `Owner` schema as a read-only string enum (`EMAIL` / `PHONE`). This drives the OpenAPI-generator to produce `OwnerDto.contactPreference` with a nested `ContactPreferenceEnum`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `contactPreference` and a helper that returns `EMAIL` when the owner has a non-blank email, otherwise `PHONE`:\n\n```java\nprotected OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum contactPreference(Owner owner) {\n    boolean hasEmail = owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank();\n    return hasEmail ? OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum.EMAIL : OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum.PHONE;\n}\n```\n\nThe two acceptance tests \u2014 `corePhoneWhenNoEmail` (expects `PHONE`) and `functionalityEmailWhenPresent` (expects `EMAIL`) \u2014 both pass.",
